    {
      "proposal_id": "if-reject-monohydrate-on-dihydrate",
      "path": "ontology_mapping.evidence[1]",
      "before": {
        "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
        "source": "MIM curation (#321/#334)",
        "notes": "identifier CHEBI:37585 -> kgmicrobe.compound:nah2po4_x_2_h2o; mapping_quality SYNONYM_MATCH -> NARROW_MATCH. The record is a hydrate of CHEBI:37585 ('sodium dihydrogenphosphate') and was sharing that term's identifier — the identity collapse MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 forbids, which made a distinct substance indistinguishable from its anhydrous parent downstream. ChEBI has no term for this hydrate and the record carries no verified CAS, so steps 1 and 2 are unavailable and step 3 applies."
      },
      "after": {
        "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
