    {
      "proposal_id": "if-reject-monohydrate-on-dihydrate",
      "path": "ontology_mapping.evidence[2]",
      "before": {
        "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
        "source": "MIM curation (#321)",
        "notes": "molecular_formula 'H2O4P.Na' -> 'H2O4P.Na.2H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:37585's ChEBI formula ('H2O4P.Na') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation."
      },
      "after": {
        "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
        "source": "MIM curation (#321)",
